AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:DOID_0050516 "o’nyong-nyong is a phrase that originated among the Acholi tribe of Uganda. It is not a proper noun and in the earliest report (1960, https://doi.org/10.1016/0035-9203(60)90025-0) was not capitalized. However, most authors have, even since those early days, capitalized the word(s). The label for this disease follows this converntion and is also capitalized.")
