# Class: obo:DOID_0060358 (multiple acyl-CoA dehydrogenase deficiency)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:type obo:ECO_0007637) Annotation(dc:type obo:ECO_0007638) Annotation(dc:type obo:ECO_0007645) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "url:http://ghr.nlm.nih.gov/condition/glutaric-acidemia-type-ii") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "url:https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glutaric_acidemia_type_2") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "url:https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12815589") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "url:https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22580358") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:DOID_0060358 "An inherited metabolic disorder characterized by the body's inability to break down proteins and fats to produce energy. It is a disorder of fatty acid, amino acid, and choline metabolism and has an autosomal recessive inheritance pattern. It has_material_basis_in mutations in the ETFA, ETFB and ETFDH genes. It presents three clinical phenotypes: a neonatal-onset form with congenital anomalies (type I), a neonatal-onset form without congenital anomalies (type II), and a late-onset form (type III). The neonatal-onset forms are usually fatal.")
