# Class: obo:DOID_10525 (double pterygium)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "url:https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/eye-disorders/conjunctival-and-scleral-disorders/pinguecula-and-pterygium") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "url:https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5340105/") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref "url:https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5598180/") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:DOID_10525 "A pterygium that is characterized by a fleshy outpouching of conjunctival growth that appears to have multiple heads or areas of bulk or origin and has_symptom multiple fleshy bumps on the surface of the eye, foreign body sensation, decreased vision, and astigmatism. Double pterygiums are more common in people prone to ocular surface injury, such as those living in sunny, hot, and dry climates. Double pterygiums progress from pinguecula.")
